   "game": "G118",
   "where": "Far Farris Raccoons at Eona Topcats, week 18",
   "text": "Rania Minamura (QB, Topcats) was flagged for unnecessary roughness with 7:05 left in the first quarter for contact to the head of Ivanei Trosemyr (RB, Raccoons). Trosemyr left for a few plays and returned. It happened in front of a national television audience.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED: on the Raccoons' ball-carrier's run, Minamura came in as the closing tackler and led with the crown of his helmet into Trosemyr's helmet while Trosemyr was already being wrapped up by a teammate. No punch, no words, no continued contact after the whistle. Trosemyr passed the concussion check and came back.\n\nSEVERITY: moderate. The league's film review found the contact was avoidable: Minamura had time to lower his target and did not. Quarterbacks are protected, but when one is the tackler he is held to the same standard as any defender. He has 1 earlier case on the desk in the last three seasons (comments about the officials, 2043 week 14: warning), nothing for dangerous play. The Topcats have been asked for their account and have not yet given one.",
